  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added authenticated acyclic private-call-graph GMP scratch frames with root-only flat allocation, borrower zeroing, whole-graph emitter validation, and unchanged dynamic fallback. Focused differential/error/fallback tests pass and H1 digest is unchanged. The allocation gate passed (99.52% fewer malloc+realloc events), but all fixed stage timing gates failed (1.26x to 1.69x versus the required 2x), so the campaign stopped without further tuning.",
    "risks": [
      "The mechanism is implemented only in the GMP C backend; fmpz parity was intentionally not attempted after the fixed performance gate failed.",
      "test:changed completed merge/build/architecture checks but its unit tier initially stopped before native preparation because this lane had no local optional sagejs_flint.node. A subsequent full test:native prepared the addon but cannot run under the campaign's hard 4 GiB address-space cap: ASan needs a multi-terabyte shadow mapping and arena tests reserve a 64 GiB virtual envelope. The focused native test passes under the 4 GiB cap against the pinned FLINT prefix.",
      "Linux x64 is measured; other supported targets retain ordinary generated fallback but were not built in this stopped campaign."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Reassess the dominant H1 costs before authorizing another campaign; allocation event count is not the main wall-time mechanism.",
      "If this mechanism is retained, integrate it independently of its failed speed gate and add platform CI plus fmpz parity as separate bounded work."
    ]
  }
